{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00601",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 0.83,
      "end_seconds": 11.05,
      "duration_seconds": 10.22,
      "text": "Mrs Okafor? Sorry about the rain, the lot is full today, so you'll want the validation stamp from me before you leave."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 12.8,
      "end_seconds": 23.92,
      "duration_seconds": 11.12,
      "text": "Oh, thank you, I parked on the street, two blocks over, I got soaked. Is this where Tobias goes, room four?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 25.37,
      "end_seconds": 33.28,
      "duration_seconds": 7.91,
      "text": "Yes, room four, the doctor's ready for you. Hi there, Tobias, love the dinosaur boots."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 34.46,
      "end_seconds": 35.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.5,
      "text": "They roar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.86,
      "end_seconds": 48.73,
      "duration_seconds": 10.87,
      "text": "Hello, you two. Come in, have a seat. What a day out there. Tobias, are those your rain boots?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 49.47,
      "end_seconds": 51.27,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "Yeah. T-Rex."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 53.32,
      "end_seconds": 57.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "Very scary. Okay, mom, what brings you in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 58.21,
      "end_seconds": 76.67,
      "duration_seconds": 18.46,
      "text": "So he's got this rash all over his tummy and a bit on his back, it started two days ago, and I thought it was the new laundry soap, but then I switched it back."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.98,
      "end_seconds": 85.99,
      "duration_seconds": 7.01,
      "text": "All right. Two days. Does it bother him, does he scratch it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 88.86,
      "end_seconds": 101.36,
      "duration_seconds": 12.5,
      "text": "Not much. Oh, and he's been cranky, but that's also because we had a birthday party Saturday, with way too much cake."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.4,
      "end_seconds": 109.26,
      "duration_seconds": 6.86,
      "text": "Ha, that'll do it. Tobias, can you show me where it is?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 110.53,
      "end_seconds": 112.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "Here. And here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.87,
      "end_seconds": 119.46,
      "duration_seconds": 5.59,
      "text": "Thank you, buddy. Mom, has he had a fever with it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 120.19,
      "end_seconds": 126.27,
      "duration_seconds": 6.08,
      "text": "No, no fever. I checked this morning, and last night."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.07,
      "end_seconds": 134.49,
      "duration_seconds": 6.42,
      "text": "And any trouble breathing, or swelling of his lips or face?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 137.32,
      "end_seconds": 148.55,
      "duration_seconds": 11.23,
      "text": "No, nothing like that, thank goodness. His face is normal. He's been chasing the dog around all morning, so he's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.64,
      "end_seconds": 156.72,
      "duration_seconds": 7.08,
      "text": "Good to know. Any medical conditions I should have on his chart?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 158.13,
      "end_seconds": 165.33,
      "duration_seconds": 7.2,
      "text": "He has asthma. Mild, since he was two. It's well controlled, mostly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 166.21,
      "end_seconds": 171.25,
      "duration_seconds": 5.04,
      "text": "Okay. And who's at home with him, besides you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 173.66,
      "end_seconds": 183.54,
      "duration_seconds": 9.88,
      "text": "My mother-in-law lives with us, so she watches him weekdays. She's obsessed with the weather, hence my umbrella."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 199.09,
      "end_seconds": 204.46,
      "duration_seconds": 5.37,
      "text": "Ha. Let me check his temperature and weight, then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.85,
      "end_seconds": 211.78,
      "duration_seconds": 5.93,
      "text": "Temperature is 37.4 °C, and his weight is 17 kg."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 213.32,
      "end_seconds": 217.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "Is that okay for four years old?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.17,
      "end_seconds": 234.02,
      "duration_seconds": 13.85,
      "text": "Right where he should be. Now, I want you to know what I'm thinking about, but I'm not putting a name on this yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 235.69,
      "end_seconds": 241.41,
      "duration_seconds": 5.72,
      "text": "That's fine. I just don't want it to get worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.98,
      "end_seconds": 264.38,
      "duration_seconds": 21.4,
      "text": "So here are the options. We could wait and watch for a few days, we could do a blood test to look at his counts, or we could get a specialist to look at the skin."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 266.18,
      "end_seconds": 269.18,
      "duration_seconds": 3.0,
      "text": "What would you pick?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.85,
      "end_seconds": 283.09,
      "duration_seconds": 11.24,
      "text": "I'd like to order a blood test today. It's quick, a tiny needle, Tobias, and it gives us information."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 284.89,
      "end_seconds": 286.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.52,
      "text": "No needle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 289.28,
      "end_seconds": 295.43,
      "duration_seconds": 6.15,
      "text": "Sweetie, it's just a tiny pinch, and there's a sticker after."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 297.19,
      "end_seconds": 306.19,
      "duration_seconds": 9.0,
      "text": "I have dinosaur stickers, actually. The lab's down the hall, I can walk you over when we're done."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 308.17,
      "end_seconds": 309.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.44,
      "text": "Dinosaur?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.97,
      "end_seconds": 322.21,
      "duration_seconds": 11.24,
      "text": "A T-Rex one, I bet. In the meantime, cool cloths on the rash feel nice, and loose cotton clothes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 324.35,
      "end_seconds": 330.82,
      "duration_seconds": 6.47,
      "text": "Okay. Cotton, cool cloths. Should I take photos of it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 331.61,
      "end_seconds": 337.83,
      "duration_seconds": 6.22,
      "text": "Yes, take a photo each morning, that'll help me see whether it's changing."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 338.99,
      "end_seconds": 344.34,
      "duration_seconds": 5.35,
      "text": "Will do. And if his lips start swelling?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 347.27,
      "end_seconds": 355.83,
      "duration_seconds": 8.56,
      "text": "Then call 911 right away, don't drive him. But I doubt it'll come to that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 357.26,
      "end_seconds": 361.83,
      "duration_seconds": 4.57,
      "text": "Okay. Thank you, doctor. And sorry for rambling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 363.2,
      "end_seconds": 370.16,
      "duration_seconds": 6.96,
      "text": "Not at all. Tobias, you were great. Stickers on the way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 370.93,
      "end_seconds": 372.8,
      "duration_seconds": 1.87,
      "text": "Bye bye."
    }
  ]
}
